  "interpretation": "The live-tool benchmark includes fresh PowerShell process startup on the native side and a persistent MCP session on the Venira side. It is a practical agent-tool-path comparison, not a raw filesystem benchmark. Component timings (Venira 1.17.0) show that raw PowerShell operations are faster for uncached reads, metadata and listings; Venira's benefit is strongest for repeated warm list/search operations and tool calls that avoid starting a fresh shell. This is one Windows machine and one run; results are not a general performance guarantee.",
